    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0443" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg347"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 27th instant, with reference to reports of legislation
                    enacted or pending in certain States of the Union, and which would place British
                    companies at a disadvantage in those States as compared with companies of other
                    nationalities.</p>
                <p>I note with satisfaction that assurances have, in some instances, been already
                    given in response to representations from your Department that the reports in
                    question are unfounded.</p>
                <p>I have duly communicated a copy of your note to Her Majesty’s principal secretary
                    of state for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reginald Tower.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
